  "result": "Perfect! All 224 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the customer statements feature:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/statements.js** \u2014 New module with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that:\n   - Validates customer exists (returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if unknown)\n   - Normalizes customer ID for consistent comparison\n   - Filters invoices for:\n     - Matching customer (after normalization)\n     - Status of 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n     - issueDate on or before asOf cutoff date\n   - Returns each invoice with: { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n   - Sorted by issueDate chronologically\n   - Calculates totalDue as sum of all due amounts\n   - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n\n**Tests added** (17 new tests):\n- Basic statement generation with multiple invoices\n- Filtering by issueDate (excludes future invoices, includes on-date invoices)\n- Including both issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Excluding draft and paid invoices\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Correct invoice fields in output\n- Due calculation for unpaid and partially paid invoices\n- totalDue as sum of individual dues\n- Error handling for unknown customer\n- Customer ID normalization (case/space handling)\n- Empty statements for customers with no unpaid invoices\n- Filtering by customer ID\n- Multiple invoices with various payment states\n\nAll 224 tests pass.",
